":"Revenue grew 45.5% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $109.5m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 64.9% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 11.8%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-33.2% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $2.9m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"About 19 months of cash at the current burn ($122.4m against $79.0m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"Debt of $211.5m against equity of $38.7m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000182115926000010/0001821159-26-000010-index.htm","accession":"0001821159-26-000010"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 1.4% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821159/000213779826000005/0002137798-26-000005-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 4.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.04,"consecutive":2,"current":0.118,"current_display":"11.8%","threshold_display":"4.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 23.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.23,"consecutive":2,"current":0.455,"current_display":"45.5%","threshold_display":"23.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":18.589,"current_display":"19 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","ed